eHash: \"438740274604\"","replacement":"sourceHash: \"438740274604\"","rationale":"I'm leaving the value unchanged, but it doesn't look like the actual source hash in the history (7d9ec399…). It may be a hash from a different scheme or an old one. Provenance metadata is controlled, so the coordinator should check it; I won't invent a value.","alternative":"","confidence":0.35,"requiresExternalEvidence":true,"audienceScope":"Repository tooling","evidence":[{"referenceId":"source","explanation":"list_translation_history shows actual sourceHash 7d9ec3992b22… and declaredSourceHash 438740274604 for the current revision."}]}],"strengths":["The frontmatter follows the repository rules: image paths use ../, inherited date is left out, and the controlled metadata is kept.","The summary anchor was correctly changed to #resumen so it points to the localized '## Resumen' heading.","The code blocks, URLs, identifiers and the source typo './kinves.js' are unchanged. Only the code comments are translated, and accurately.","The core technical claims are faithful: aliasing, the export default/const restriction, and support for classes. Terminology matches Spanish MDN ('exportación nombrada' / 'por defecto').","The table keeps the same rows, the checkmark pattern and the MDX <section> wrapper.","'Odio ser quien te lo diga, ¡pero espera a ver lo que pueden hacer las variables!' keeps the author's sarcasm naturally."],"sourceConcerns":["The Summary table's checkmarks don't match its Pattern text. Row 3 says 'Default export + multiple private un-exported functions' but marks Named ✅. Row 4 says 'Multiple named exports' but marks Named ❌. The translation keeps these as written; the author should review.","'./kinves.js' looks like a typo for 'knives'. It's inside code, so it was correctly kept as is.","'AirBnb' is usually written 'Airbnb'. This is a minor source stylization and is kept."]}
